Howdy -- bears_2param_standard_fast() and it's relatives are old functions that aren't really being actively maintained.  You should use bears_optim_run() like in the script:

http://phylo.wikidot.com/biogeobears#toc12

bears_optim_run() will run any of the models, you specify which one by setting the params_table in BioGeoBEARS_run_object$BioGeoBEARS_model_object.

I just ran your data without problems with bears_optim_run (see attached), but if you see this problem again:

"Function returned is infinite or NA"

...it is probably this problem/solution:

https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/biogeobears/_bMVH521KHM

Cheers!
Nick

